<!doctype html><html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>No CL and CL: complete comparison</title><style>body{max-width:1150px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 20px;font:17px Arial;line-height:1.5;color:#16324f}img{max-width:100%}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left}.note{background:#fff2dd;padding:16px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:bold;margin:16px 0}</style><h1>No CL versus CL: complete validation comparison</h1><p class="note">All replay controllers are displayed even if they fail selection. . DIAGNOSTIC: initial quality did not meet every reference limit in the source run. No winner is selected; all fixed methods are measured, including failures. Current initial quality: 14/15 validation references pass. A lower average over surviving episodes must not hide failed episodes.</p><p>Case A = 90%, B = 60%, C = 30%, D = 45% reference muscle capacity. Training order A to B to C to D, then frozen return to A. Seed 42. These are validation results, not reserved-test results.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Controller</th><th>Completed</th><th>Failed</th><th>Accuracy passed</th><th>RMSE, completed ONLY (deg)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>No CL</td><td>15/15</td><td>0</td><td>6/15</td><td>3.3862</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Accuracy limits: motion RMSE ≤ 0.5 degrees and motion peak error ≤ 2.0 degrees. Failures have no valid final full-episode RMSE. Means shown above include completed episodes only.</p><h2>All Methods Summary</h2><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><h2>Every Reference</h2><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><h2>Learning And Adaptation</h2><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><h2>Reference 01</h2><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><h2>Every remaining reference: No CL and every CL candidate</h2><details><summary>Reference 02</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 03</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 04</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 05</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 06</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 07</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 08</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 09</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 10</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 11</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 12</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 13</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 14</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><details><summary>Reference 15</summary><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></details><h2>How to interpret the curves</h2><p>Black dashed: reference; gray: before adaptation; orange: No CL; blue, green and purple: CL beta 1, 4 and 16. A trace that ends early is a failed simulation, not successful tracking. All methods use matching reference IDs. Showing a candidate is separate from selecting it as scientifically acceptable.</p><p>HTML is self-contained. PDF and PNG figures are also saved separately in figures/. CSV files contain all metrics. No weights, data splits, selection limits or old measurements were changed to produce this comparison.</p><p><a href="TECHNICAL_REPORT.html">Detailed technical report: all inputs, architecture, losses, training and data counts</a></p></html>